<title>USA: Mining investors keen on Latin America.</title>
<headline>Mining investors keen on Latin America.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mining investors are keen on Latin America because of the region's rich potential, a mining consultant said on Monday.</p>
<p>In the period between 1995 and 1999 world production of gold will rise 15 percent, but production in Latin America will increase 39 percent, Don East, Principal, Knight Piesold told the Western Mining Conference here.</p>
<p>Later, East told Reuters that gold production in South Africa will decline and U.S. production will level off.</p>
<p>Latin America produces 12 percent of the world's gold, 40 percent of the silver and 39 percent of the world's copper.</p>
</text>
